# Authentication System – MediMind

## 1. Purpose of this document
This document explains how Authentication is implemented in the MediMind project.  
It is meant to help any team member continue development without breaking the authentication flow.

---

## 2. Authentication Overview
MediMind uses Firebase Authentication for:

- Email & Password registration  
- Email & Password login  
- Google Sign-In  
- Email verification  
- Password reset  
- User session handling  

Authentication logic is centralized inside:

`lib/auth/service/auth_service.dart`

IMPORTANT:  
- UI screens must NOT directly use FirebaseAuth.  
- All authentication logic must go through AuthService.

---

## 3. Tools & Technologies
- Flutter (Dart)  
- Firebase Authentication  
- Cloud Firestore  
- Google Sign-In  

Dependencies (pubspec.yaml):

- firebase_core  
- firebase_auth  
- cloud_firestore  
- google_sign_in  

---

## 4. Architecture Structure
Authentication is separated into:

**UI Layer**
- LoginScreen  
- RegisterScreen  
- AuthGate  

**Service Layer**
- AuthService  

IMPORTANT:  
- Business logic must remain inside AuthService.  
- UI must only call service methods.

---

## 5. User Registration (Email & Password)

Implemented in:  
`RegisterScreen → AuthService.signUp()`

Registration flow:

1. User enters:
   - Full Name  
   - Email  
   - Password  
   - Confirm Password  

2. Validations:
   - Email format validation (RegEx)  
   - Password match validation  
   - Password strength validation:
     - Minimum 8 characters  
     - At least 1 uppercase letter  
     - At least 1 number  

3. Firebase account creation:

`_auth.createUserWithEmailAndPassword()`

4. After successful creation:

A Firestore document is created in:

Collection: `users`  
Document ID: `user.uid`

Stored fields:
- uid  
- fullName  
- email  
- profilePhotoUrl  
- notificationsEnabled  
- createdAt (serverTimestamp)  
- lastLogin (serverTimestamp)  

5. Email verification is sent:
`user.sendEmailVerification()`

6. User is immediately signed out.

IMPORTANT:
- Users CANNOT access the app without verifying email.  
- Firestore document is created during registration.

---

## 6. Email Verification Enforcement

Email verification is enforced in:
- LoginScreen  
- AuthGate  

Flow:

After login:
- User is reloaded using `user.reload()`  
- If `emailVerified == false`:
  - Login is blocked  
  - A dialog is shown  
  - User can resend verification email  
  - User can sign out  

AuthGate checks:
- If `user.emailVerified == true` → MainScreen  
- If false → LoginScreen  

IMPORTANT:
- Email verification is mandatory.

---

## 7. Login (Email & Password)

Implemented in:  
`LoginScreen → AuthService.signIn()`

Login flow:

1. Email format validation  
2. Firebase login:
`_auth.signInWithEmailAndPassword()`  

3. After successful login:
- Firestore updates `lastLogin → serverTimestamp`

Error handling includes:
- invalid-email  
- wrong-password  
- user-not-found  
- user-disabled  
- too-many-requests  

IMPORTANT:
- Raw Firebase errors must NOT be exposed to the UI.  
- All errors are handled inside AuthService.

---

## 8. Google Sign-In

Implemented in:  
`AuthService.signInWithGoogle()`

Flow:
1. `GoogleSignIn().signIn()`  
2. Retrieve authentication tokens  
3. Create Firebase credential:
   `GoogleAuthProvider.credential()`  
4. Sign in with:
   `_auth.signInWithCredential()`  

Firestore behavior:

If user does NOT exist:
- Create new user document  
- provider: "google"  
- createdAt  
- lastLogin  

If user exists:
- Update lastLogin only  

IMPORTANT:
- Google users are stored in the same `users` collection.

---

## 9. Password Reset

Implemented in:  
`AuthService.sendPasswordResetEmail()`

Flow:
- User enters email  
- Firebase sends reset email  

Security rule:
- No error is shown if email does not exist  

IMPORTANT:
- Do NOT reveal whether an email is registered.

---

## 10. Session Management (AuthGate)

AuthGate listens to:

`_auth.authStateChanges()`

Behavior:
- If connectionState == waiting → Show loading indicator  
- If user exists AND emailVerified == true → Navigate to MainScreen  
- Otherwise → Navigate to LoginScreen  

IMPORTANT:
- AuthGate controls all session redirection.

---

## 11. Firestore Structure (Users Collection)

Collection: `users`  
Document ID: `uid`

Fields:
- uid  
- fullName  
- email  
- profilePhotoUrl  
- notificationsEnabled  
- createdAt  
- lastLogin  
- provider (Google users only)

IMPORTANT:
- Collection name must remain `users`.

---

## 12. What must NOT be changed

- Collection name: `users`  
- AuthService method structure  
- Email verification enforcement  
- AuthGate logic  
- Firestore field names  
- Google Sign-In integration flow  

Changing these may break:
- Login  
- Registration  
- Session handling  

---

## 13. Git & Branching

Authentication system is implemented in branch:

`feature/authentication-system`

All future authentication-related features must be built on top of this structure.